# ButterFi application Kconfig.
#
# NOTE: because this app Kconfig exists, Zephyr uses it as the application's
# root Kconfig — it MUST `source "Kconfig.zephyr"` at the end or the entire
# Zephyr Kconfig tree disappears.

config BUTTERFI_LOG_CDC
	bool "Expose a second USB CDC ACM for console + LOG (field debug)"
	default n
	help
	  When enabled, app.overlay instantiates a second USB CDC ACM interface
	  (cdc_acm_uart1) and routes the Zephyr console + LOG backend to it, so
	  Sidewalk/Zephyr logs surface as a second /dev/ttyACM for field debugging
	  with no SWD probe.

	  Leave disabled (the default) for student units: the browser's Web Serial
	  device picker then shows exactly ONE device — the ButterFi runtime port —
	  so a young student cannot pick the wrong one. Enable it via
	  prj.sidewalk-log.conf, which also turns the console/UART LOG backend on.

source "Kconfig.zephyr"
